+# Incidents brief
+
+## 11 August: data intake stall, full database disk
+
+**Impact:** about 2.5 hours overnight without new data; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+
+**Cause:** one malformed batch jammed data intake; its retries filled the database disk with logs, stopping writes.
+
+**Fix:** a restart setting the batch aside, then non-disruptive database cleanup and log pruning.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Disk alert at 80%: no owner named; open.
+- Paging rules (primary, secondary, then Mara; escalate after 15 unanswered minutes): Elif, Sunil; done.
+- Check handbook for the old 30-minute figure: Mara; open.
+- Stop bad batches jamming intake: Jonas; open.
+
+## 21 September: public API outage
+
+**Impact:** 47 minutes, Monday morning; nearly all customer connections refused.
+
+**Cause:** the API certificate expired; automatic renewal had silently failed for three weeks (outdated access token).
+
+**Fix:** certificate renewed, API restarted.
+
+**Follow-ups:**
+- Repair renewal job, alert on failures: no owner named; done.
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry: no owner named; open.
+- Alert on days to expiry: no owner named; open.
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist: no owner named; open.
+- Incident handlers log steps live: everyone; agreed practice.
+
+Open: not recorded done in meeting notes (to 30 September).
